                                  iNSTALLATION
                               _ ___        ___ _
                                   \________/
                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _
                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///
                                      \\//
                                       \/










  mAKE  A  DIR  named:   "DOORS:SCEPTIC" and copy the dir "F!-LAST" to it.

  FNISHED ...





  SAD-LAST.cfg
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~

  BULLFILE	= Outputfile
  HEADER	= Header (ascii???)
  ENTRIES	= Number of last callers entrys in the bullfile
  TIMEKIND	= WHICH TIME TO SHOW ... ONLINE or TRANSFER time used!
  SHOWLEGEND    = Show ACTIVITIES description on(1)/off(0)
  PAGERECOG	= "<key which your pager always print to callerslog>"
  SCANRECOG	= "<key which your confscan always print to callerslog>"
  ACCORECOG	= "<key /X writes to callerslog if account editing!>"
                  Normaly it`s "Account Maintenance" but you may have
                  a patched version? there are out some of them!

  eg:	BULLFILE	= "doors:sceptic/F!-LAST/SAD-LAST.bull"
  	HEADER		= "doors:Sceptic/F!-LAST/SAD-LAST.header"
  	ENTRIES		= 10
  	TIMEKIND	= T
        SHOWLEGEND	= 1
  	PAGERECOG	= "Operator Paged at"
  	SCANRECOG	= "Directory Scan with AquaScan"
  	ACCORECOG	= "Account Maintenance on"


  Get your LOGOFF BATCH open and add the followng line:

  -> cUT <-------------------------------------------------------------------

  doors:sceptic/sad-last.exe <node>

  -------------------------------------------------------------------> cUT <-

  eg: doors:sceptic/sad-last.exe 1    for node 1




   Now load the "SAD-LAST.header" file and edit your personal header beeing
                       placed right above the outputfile!

                                  THAT`S ALL!










